main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ non-type value pack Trait<Us>::value\.\.\. expands to 2 elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5 + [temp.res] (two-phase).  A pack expansion
whose pattern is a NON-TYPE value dependent on the pack (`Trait<Us>::value...`),
used as the template-argument list of a template-id in a FUNCTION TEMPLATE's
body, is resolved abstractly at the function template's DEFINITION (pack unbound)
and is NOT re-instantiated concretely when the function template is instantiated
-- only an abstract `box<Non_Type0>` is produced, so `box<...>::n` is left
unconstrained instead of 2.  The TYPE-id form `box<sz<Us>...>::n`, a bare pack
`box<Us...>::n`, and a nested type-id all re-instantiate correctly; only the
non-type `::value` pack expansion fails (verified by instrumentation: the type-id
form re-instantiates while the `::value` form yields only `box<Non_Type0>`).  No
class template or alias is needed.  This is the residual blocker beneath the
fixed two-parallel-pack member-alias expansion
(cpp11_alias_template_parallel_pack) and for std::tuple's _TupleConstraints
(`__and_<is_X<_Types,_UTypes>...>::value`).  Flip to CORE once such a non-type
value pack expansion in a function-template body is re-instantiated concretely at
the point of instantiation.
